BT /F2 17 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 736.0 Tm (CIVICPULSE API GUIDE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 714.0 Tm (Endpoints first. Plain-language bullet explanations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 679.0 Tm (AUTHENTICATION: HOW THE USERS WORK) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 660.0 Tm (There are four user role types in the code. This is not the number of registered accounts. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 648.0 Tm (actual account count depends on the current database; it cannot be determined from the source) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 636.0 Tm (code or this guide.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 619.0 Tm (- resident - the default role for anyone who registers. Can submit, browse and follow reports, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 607.0 Tm (  use personal notifications.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 591.0 Tm (- verifier - reviews reports, verifies or rejects them, assigns verified cases, reviews duplicate) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 579.0 Tm (  suggestions, and can list authority users.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 563.0 Tm (- authority - works on assigned cases, moves them to in_progress and resolved, views staff) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 551.0 Tm (  analytics, and can list authority users.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 535.0 Tm (- admin - staff role with broad access, including user listing, duplicate decisions, analytics and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 523.0 Tm (  hotspot recomputation. Admin accounts are provisioned separately.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 502.0 Tm (SIGN-IN FLOW) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 483.0 Tm (- Registering creates a resident account only; a submitted role is not used. Email is normalized,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 471.0 Tm (  passwords are stored as hashes, and duplicate emails are rejected.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 455.0 Tm (- Login checks the email and password, then returns a signed JWT token and user profile. The token) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 443.0 Tm (  lasts 7 days.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 427.0 Tm (- For protected endpoints, send Authorization: Bearer <token>. The backend validates the token and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 415.0 Tm (  reloads the user and role from the database on each request.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 399.0 Tm (- 401 means the request is unauthenticated \(missing/invalid/expired token\). 403 means signed in,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 387.0 Tm (  but the role is not allowed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 371.0 Tm (- Roles are not self-selected at signup. Staff users can be created with the Flask CLI command) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 359.0 Tm (  `flask create-user` and the required role.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 343.0 Tm (- There is no live API route to change a user's role. The OpenAPI document lists PATCH) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 331.0 Tm (  /users/{id}/role, but the Flask app does not register it.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 313.0 Tm (POST /api/v1/auth/register  |  Public) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 300.0 Tm (- Input: name, email, password \(at least 8 characters\), optional area_id. Success: 201 with) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 288.0 Tm (  {token, user}; invalid data: 422; existing email: 409.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 270.0 Tm (POST /api/v1/auth/login  |  Public) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 257.0 Tm (- Input: email and password. Success: 200 with {token, user}; incorrect email or password returns) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 245.0 Tm (  401 with the same message.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 227.0 Tm (GET /api/v1/auth/me  |  Signed-in user) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 214.0 Tm (- Returns the current user's profile from the authenticated token and database.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.4 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 196.0 Tm (GET /api/v1/users  |  Verifier, authority, admin) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 183.0 Tm (- Admins can list users and filter by role. Verifiers and authorities only receive authority) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 171.0 Tm (  users, with email removed. Results are paginated.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 155.0 Tm (- This route does not return an account total. To know how many accounts exist, count records in) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.2 Tf 1 0 0 1 48 143.0 Tm (  the users table or add a dedicated count/reporting route.) Tj ET
